# CEG: lampy-installer — Lampy full installer
# Repo: cosbykit-afk/lampy-installer
# Standing: the installer must keep working for everybody else and for
# future releases — never hardcoded to Kit's machine or the current release.
#
# v1.1.10 corrections (2026-09-28, verified against install.ps1/uninstall.ps1
# at commit 237e12d and lampy-slim.nsi):
# - Installer is per-user; the admin requirement was removed from install.ps1
#   in c4b0c3f (2026-09-27) and from uninstall.ps1 in 237e12d (v1.1.10).
#   lampy-slim.nsi uses RequestExecutionLevel user. c4/f1 deleted.
# - Repair with an existing distro skips the download AND the import entirely
#   ($tarball = "SKIP"); the bundle is never used. Old e4 deleted.
# - Repair without an existing distro does NOT refuse; it downloads and
#   imports fresh. Old f5 was wrong; replaced by e10.
# - Uninstall only removes the scheduled task if its command line contains
#   "-d <DistroName>" (v1.1.10 safety fix). New input c10, effects e8/e9.
# - uninstall.ps1 does not branch on user_data (c7); it always removes the
#   distro (which holds the data) after confirmation. c7 dropped from
#   uninstall rules. REQ-LI-005 corrected: uninstall DELETES user data.
# - Edge: if WSL itself is not installed, install.ps1 throws and asks for a
#   one-time admin run to enable the WSL feature. That is a precondition
#   failure, not a modeled flow variable.

[PAGE]
Installer flows: install (fresh/upgrade), repair, uninstall,
verify-bundle, set-passwords. Grounded in install.ps1, uninstall.ps1,
lampy.nsi / lampy-slim.nsi, verify-bundle.py, set-passwords.py.

[INPUTS]
c1 = flow : install | repair | uninstall | verify | passwords
c2 = bundle_present : no | yes
c3 = existing_install : no | yes
c5 = bundle_hash : match | mismatch
c6 = target_dir : missing | empty | occupied
c7 = user_data : absent | present
c8 = passwords_set : no | yes
c9 = confirm : no | yes
c10 = scheduled_task : absent | this_distro | other_distro

[CONSTRAINTS]

[SUCCESS]
e1 = fresh install completes and services register
e1 <= c1=install AND c2=yes AND c3=no AND c5=match AND c6=empty
e2 = upgrade install completes and existing user data is preserved
e2 <= c1=install AND c2=yes AND c3=yes AND c5=match AND c7=present
e3 = repair with existing distro skips download and import, re-runs configuration (v1.1.10)
e3 <= c1=repair AND c3=yes
e5 = uninstall removes distro, install dir, and its own scheduled task on confirmation (v1.1.10)
e5 <= c1=uninstall AND c9=yes AND c10=this_distro
e6 = verify-bundle passes when every hash matches the manifest
e6 <= c1=verify AND c5=match
e7 = set-passwords writes fresh credentials
e7 <= c1=passwords AND c8=no
e8 = uninstall removes distro and install dir but leaves a foreign scheduled task (v1.1.10 safety)
e8 <= c1=uninstall AND c9=yes AND c10=other_distro
e9 = uninstall removes distro and install dir when no scheduled task exists
e9 <= c1=uninstall AND c9=yes AND c10=absent
e10 = repair without an existing distro downloads the bundle and imports fresh
e10 <= c1=repair AND c3=no

[FAIL]
f2 = fresh install refuses an occupied directory that is not an install
f2 <= c1=install AND c3=no AND c6=occupied
f3 = verify-bundle fails on hash mismatch
f3 <= c1=verify AND c5=mismatch
f4 = uninstall aborts on missing confirmation (distro and data left untouched)
f4 <= c1=uninstall AND c9=no

[REQUIREMENTS]
REQ-LI-001 : fresh install on an empty target dir completes with services registered -> e1
REQ-LI-002 : upgrade install preserves existing user data -> e2
REQ-LI-003 : repair with existing distro skips download and import, re-runs config -> e3
REQ-LI-004 : repair without an existing distro downloads and imports fresh (never refuses) -> e10
REQ-LI-005 : uninstall requires explicit confirmation; deletes the distro and its data -> e5, e8, e9, f4
REQ-LI-006 : verify-bundle passes on matching hashes, fails on mismatch -> e6, f3
REQ-LI-007 : set-passwords writes fresh credentials -> e7
REQ-LI-008 : install refuses occupied non-install dirs; installer is per-user, no admin required -> f2
REQ-LI-009 : uninstall removes the scheduled task only if it belongs to this distro -> e5, e8, e9
REQ-LI-010 : no machine-specific paths and no release pins anywhere in the installer sources -> e1
